WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.234
-It is so great to see you.
You look fantastic.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.400
-Thank you so much.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.868
-I want to congratulate you,
because last time

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.501
you were on our show -- shortly
after you were on our show,

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.167
you did a one-woman play
off-Broadway

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:13.934
and got nominated for
all these awards for acting.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.234
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.067
-It's a big deal.
-Thank you.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Can I just say that --

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.601
-That was really amazing and
challenging for me.

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:24.868
The most challenging thing
I've ever done in my career.

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.501
I mean, being -- And,
of course, a dream come true,

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:31.267
because an actress,
Mexican actress,

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:35.000
off-Broadway show,
you know, like,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.801
talking about my own country,
about "Las Muertas de Juárez"

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.467
in English, which is not
my first language --

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.634
that was something
that I couldn't say no.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.367
But then, when I said yes,
I wanted to die.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.734
I was like, "How am I going to
pull this off?"

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.968
I thought I was not going to be
able to really --

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.334
to pull it off.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.634
And they say I'm brave and
I'm tough and this and that

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.033
because I went to see El Chapo.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.300
That was a walk in the park.
I mean...

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.400
-Really? Compared to this?
-Of course.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.968
-Well, how many characters
were in --

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.501
-14.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.300
-Kate, why would you do this
to yourself?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.701
I mean, really.
-I don't know.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.534
It's painful even now.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.467
-But you crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.767
-Can I just say, you became
the first Mexican actor

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.534
to be nominated for
three American theater awards

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.033
in a single season.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.501
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.234
-That is --
-Thank you.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.367
-In history.
-Yes.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.567
-In history.
-Yes.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.767
-"La Reina."

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.334
Can we talk about "La Reina,"
the Queen?

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.968
-Of course.
-Yeah. You're back.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:33.601
Explain the story behind this,
because I know you came out.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.868
You had one season.
It was a giant hit.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.501
And then you
didn't come back for like

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.968
another couple years.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.100
-10 years.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.834
The first season,
and then, 10 years later,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.200
we did the second season.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.868
And I was like nobody is going
to remember "La Reina."

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.167
-But why did it take
that long to do?

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.767
-Because it was only one book.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.067
So, it's based on a
novel written by

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:55.267
this amazing author from Spain
called Arturo Pérez-Reverte.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.567
So it was only one book.

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.567
Why do a second season?
It was a great hit.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.767
I was like, "Let's just leave it
as it is, and it's great.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.467
But then, you know,
they get greedy, you know?

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.167
Those things --
-Yeah.

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:08.634
Yeah. It's making
a profit, yeah.

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.734
-And it was again a super hit.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:15.901
And we -- You know, we were
number 1 in its time slot.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.934
NBC, CBS,
like, we were the number 1.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.968
Which is amazing to be --
I mean,

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.467
it's amazing to be right here
sitting with you,

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.968
promoting a
Spanish-speaking show.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.100
I think that's amazing.
It wouldn't happen before.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.934
-Yeah, I agree.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.968
I'm happy about that.
-I appreciate that.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.300
I appreciate that.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.601
So, now we are doing Season 3.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.934
And this one comes --
Like, it's the most ambitious.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.234
-By the way, it's gorgeous.

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.200
Who is it behind it?
Telemundo and...

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.701
-Telemundo, Netflix.
-And Netflix.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.501
Yeah, you can tell
there's some money behind this.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.534
-There's a lot of money.
I mean, I can --

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.601
-It's really big budget.
-I know.

00:02:49.601 --> 00:02:51.634
And it's 60 episodes,
and each episode

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.067
is better than the other one.

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:55.901
I'm like, "Oh, my God, this is
like a movie, every single one."

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.400
So I'm very excited for this --
-The locations.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.567
-We got the Emmy
on the last season.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.534
-That's right. Congratulations.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.200
-Did that feel good?
-Yeah.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.434
-That's got to feel good, right?
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.567
The International Emmys.
So, that's what I'm saying.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.701
We're getting there, you know?

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:13.601
And Spanish-speaking shows,
actresses,

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.234
Mexican actresses --
we're getting there.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.868
-You're breaking through.
-Yes.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.701
-Can we say what's happening --

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.901
what's going to happen
this new season?

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.467
-We're staying away from
the narco-trafficking thing,

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.534
which I think is amazing.

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.767
Now it's more of
a political thriller.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.167
Action. There's a lot of action.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.100
There's -- We went to
five different countries.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.067
You're going to see
a Latin America

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:35.200
that if you are not
Latin American,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.801
you're going know what
Latin America is made of.

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.334
And if you're Latin American,
you're going to be

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:40.934
so proud,
because we're going to show

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:44.434
the magnificent Latin America
that we have.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.133
-Yes!
-Yes, yes.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.834
And amazing places.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:52.200
We went to Bolivia.
We went to Peru.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.868
We went to Argentina,
to Mexico, and Colombia.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.467
So, yes.
-Oh, get ready.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.267
You put the work in,
and it is fantastic.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.801
I'm so happy that
you came back to our show.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.501
-Yes, thank you.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.701
Here's Kate del Castillo
in the new season of

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:06.934
"La Reina del Sur."

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:07.934
Take a look.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.834
-Let's go, let's go!
-Move, move!

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.167
-Come on, let's go!

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.601
-Hold your fire!
I want her alive!

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.400
Let's go! Go, go!

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.367
-I mean, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.834
You are just the best. Come on.

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:53.000
Kate del Castillo, everybody!

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.501
"La Reina del Sur"

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:58.634
premieres October 18th
at 9:00 p.m. on Telemundo.

